 The pages under `docs/` are this repository's source of truth for people and coding agents. This page says which page
 owns each fact; read it before writing one.
+
+## Kinds
+
+- [Features](features/README.md) are reference pages for what a unit of behavior does: its rules, examples and known
+  limits with workarounds. Reasons confined to that feature belong here; link any decision records that shape it.
+- [Decisions](adrs/README.md) explain foundation choices whose reversal changes more than one feature or module.
+  Each record gives the context, options and why they lost or won, decision and consequences. A choice confined to
+  one feature belongs on that feature's page instead.
+- [Runbooks](runbooks/README.md) give instructions for one operational trigger, with steps and the expected output
+  that tells the operator each step worked.
+- [Architecture](architecture.md) explains the system's parts and how they connect, linking decision records for
+  the reasons behind structural choices.
+
+The [glossary](glossary.md) owns the terms used throughout these pages and the synonyms to avoid.
